@page "/apply"

<PageTitle>Apply for a loan</PageTitle>

<h1>Apply for a loan</h1>

<div class="alert alert-secondary">Step 1: the application form goes here.</div>

@*
TODO(step 1): the application form.

 - Pick a render mode. With no @rendermode this page is static server-rendered: an EditForm
   still works (it posts back; use [SupplyParameterFromForm] and give the form a FormName),
   but @onclick handlers silently do nothing. With @rendermode InteractiveServer, events run
   over a SignalR circuit and you get live validation as the user types.

 - Form model (a class in this project, e.g. Components/Models/ApplicationForm.cs) with
   DataAnnotations: [Required] name, [EmailAddress] email, [Range] amount 1 000–500 000,
   term 6–120 months, income and expenses >= 0. Render <DataAnnotationsValidator /> and
   <ValidationSummary /> inside the EditForm.

 - On valid submit:
     var application = LoanApplication.Submit(..., TimeProvider.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime);
     await Repository.InsertAsync(application);
     Navigation.NavigateTo($"/applications/{application.Id}");
   Inject ILoanApplicationRepository, TimeProvider and NavigationManager.

 - In step 2 the end of that flow changes: after inserting, send ProcessApplication with
   ICommandSender (session id = application id, message id = a SubmissionId generated when
   the form is first rendered, so a double-click is caught by duplicate detection).
*@
